  "problem": "Find the global extrema of the function $f(x,y)=(x-2)^{2}+y$ on the closed region \n$D=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 2x\\}.$ \nYou are given  that $f$ has no critical points in the region and on the boundary of the region,  the points that can possibly give rise to extreme values are $(0,0)$, $(2,4),$ and  $(1,1).$",
